From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PS5 Mesa port <ps5-mesa@localhost>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:31:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] glapi: libGL.so.1 for EGL without GLX

With -Dglx=disabled -Degl=enabled -Dopengl=true there was no library that
exports the OpenGL API: a program could create an OpenGL context through EGL
but had to fetch every function with eglGetProcAddress, and SDL, which
dlopen()s libGL.so.1 (or libOpenGL.so.0) for an OpenGL context on EGL, could
not create one.

Build libGL.so.1 in that configuration (without glvnd): every function of
Mesa's dispatch, each calling the current context's dispatch table through
shared-glapi, as libGLESv2's entry points do; gl.pc names it. The four
*IndirectCount functions, whose parameters Mesa's XML declares differently
from <GL/glext.h>, are left out, as GLX's libGL leaves them out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ZqjJDSiP9GQFUidfnxiHF
---
 src/mesa/glapi/opengl/gen_symbols.py | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 src/mesa/glapi/opengl/libgl_public.c | 19 +++++++++++
 src/mesa/glapi/opengl/meson.build    | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/meson.build                      |  4 +++
 4 files changed, 103 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/mesa/glapi/opengl/gen_symbols.py
